1. What is File Handling in Java?
    File handling in java is performing various operations on files, such as:
        Creating a file
        Writing data into a file
        Reading data from a file.
        Appending data
        Deleting a file
    
    Example:
        Instead of storing a student's name temporarily in a variable, we can store it in a file so it remains even after the program ends.
    Example file (students.txt)
            Ravi
            Priya
            Arun
        Your Java program can read or write this file.

All the classes related to File handling in java is available in the java.io package

Common file handling classes:
        | Class            | Purpose                        |
        | ---------------- | ------------------------------ |
        | `File`           | Represents a file or directory |
        | `FileWriter`     | Writes data to file            |
        | `FileReader`     | Reads characters from file     |
        | `BufferedWriter` | Writes efficiently             |
        | `BufferedReader` | Reads efficiently              |
        | `PrintWriter`    | Easy formatted writing         |
        | `Scanner`        | Reads file like user input     |

