| Direction                        | Name             |
| -------------------------------- | ---------------- |
| Data **coming into the program** | **InputStream**  | - FileInputStream
| Data **leaving the program**     | **OutputStream** | - FileOutputStream
With FileInputStream / FileOutputStream:
    You work with bytes
        So:
            reading → cast byte to char (char)
            writing → convert char to byte getBytes()

Golden rule:
    InputStream / OutputStream → bytes
    Reader / Writer → characters

Important points:
    ✔ FileInputStream reads bytes
    ✔ FileOutputStream writes bytes
    ✔ Used for binary files
    Refer FileInputStream and FileOutputStream folder (FIS & FOS folders) for image and pdf reading and writing --> 
    Examples:
        images
        audio
        video
        pdf
    For text writing, usually better to use
        FileWriter
        BufferedWriter
    because they work with characters instead of bytes.

FileInputStream methods summary:
    | Method         | Purpose                             |
    | -------------- | ----------------------------------- |
    | `read()`       | reads **one byte**                  |
    | `read(byte[])` | reads **multiple bytes into array** |
    | `available()`  | returns **remaining bytes**         |
    | `close()`      | closes the stream                   |


FileOutputStream methods summary:
    | Method                            | Purpose                   |
    | --------------------------------- | ------------------------- |
    | `write(int b)`                    | write one byte            |
    | `write(byte[] b)`                 | write entire byte array   |
    | `write(byte[] b,int off,int len)` | write part of byte array  |
    | `flush()`                         | force write buffered data |
    | `close()`                         | close the stream          |




